Dict{"step_by_step_thinking": "The patient is a 39-year-old man with recurrent headaches, unconsciousness, and generalized tonic-clonic seizures. His history includes alcohol use and multiple sexual partners. The MRI shows bilateral, confluent, edematous lesions in the cerebral white matter with punctate hemorrhages. The brain biopsy reveals perivascular clusters of lymphocytes. These clinical features are most consistent with the description of acute disseminated encephalomyelitis (ADEM) in the provided documents.

